window.docContents[213].resolve({"/Improper-integrals/3___2-Continuous-primitives-across-the-exceptional-set/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Improper-integrals--3___2-Continuous-primitives-across-the-exceptional-set":{"contents":"IsFiniteExceptionalPrimitive g k S F packages a primitive normalized by F k = 0. The function\nF is continuous on [k,+∞), and on every compact interval avoiding S its increment is the\nintegral of g.\n\n\n\nThe improper integral has value I exactly when such a normalized primitive tends to I at\n+∞. This is the bridge between local antiderivative identities and the global improper value.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Improper integrals","header":"3.2 Continuous primitives across the exceptional set","id":"/Improper-integrals/3___2-Continuous-primitives-across-the-exceptional-set/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Improper-integrals--3___2-Continuous-primitives-across-the-exceptional-set"}});